SUMMARY:Deadline: BFI NETWORK England: Early Development Fund (GBP 3\,000-5
 \,000 treatment awards for debut long-form writers)
DESCRIPTION:BFI NETWORK's Early Development Fund supports writers at the ve
 ry start of a debut long-form project: those who do not yet have a first d
 raft of a script (or the equivalent format for immersive work). Stage one 
 awards GBP 3\,000 to 5\,000 to produce an initial treatment setting out st
 ory\, characters\, themes and structure\, plus related materials such as a
  mood board or other visual content.\n\nOrganisation: BFI NETWORK (BFI\, N
 ational Lottery funding)\nLocation: England. Writers must be based in Engl
 and.\nAward: GBP 3\,000 to 5\,000 per project to develop a treatment (stag
 e one). Projects completed to schedule can then apply for second-stage fun
 ding to write a full first draft. National Lottery funding\; no applicatio
 n fee stated.\nDuration: Treatment stage\, then optional first-draft stage
 \n\nMore: https://www.bfi.org.uk/get-funding-support/bfi-network/bfi-netwo
 rk-funding-finder/bfi-network-england-early-development-fund?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.bfi.org.uk/get-funding-support/bfi-network/bfi-network-fund
 ing-finder/bfi-network-england-early-development-fund?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:England. Writers must be based in England.
END:VEVENT
